  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>f988fa6c78719c314ff520ac135085c2</srcmd5>
    <version>0.19.0</version>
    <time>1786543881</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.19.0

Three upstream releases since 0.16.0. The bulk of the work is output
control on the read tools, aimed at not flooding an MCP client's context
on busy bugs: bug_comments, bug_history and list_attachments gained
filtering and limits, and bug_info gained native include_fields /
exclude_fields that are forwarded unchanged to the Bug.get API. New
get_bug_flags and update_bug_flag tools cover reading and setting bug
flags such as needinfo. Two real fixes: non-JSON Bugzilla responses (a
proxy or WAF returning HTML) now report the HTTP status, content type
and a body snippet instead of a bare JSONDecodeError, and Bugzilla's
integer is_private/is_obsolete flags are coerced to booleans in
download_attachment results, which was failing FastMCP schema
validation.

0.17.0 added anonymous access -- the server now runs with no Bugzilla
API key and sends no credentials -- and renamed the CLI options
(--api-key-header becomes --mcp-auth-header, --api-key becomes
--bugzilla-api-key, --use-auth-header becomes --bugzilla-auth-mode
bearer). The old names still work and log a deprecation warning; I
verified both sets are present in --help on the built RPM. 0.18.0 is a
reissue of 0.17.0 after a premature PyPI release.

Packaging: the only spec change is the fastmcp floor, 3.4.2 -&gt; 3.4.6,
matching upstream's own dependency (upstream pins fastmcp==3.4.6; the
floor is the usual downstream relaxation, as the previous 3.4.2 floor
was for upstream's ==3.4.2). Factory already carries fastmcp 3.4.7 and
the local build was done against it, so this resolves in Factory today.

Verified on aarch64: build green, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings, %check
(import mcp_bugzilla) passes against fastmcp 3.4.7, and mcp-bugzilla
--help runs from the installed RPM. spec-cleaner --remove-groups
--pkgconfig --perl --tex is a no-op.

One note so it is not mistaken for a regression: devel:tools currently
shows this unresolvable on openSUSE_Tumbleweed because that snapshot
still serves fastmcp 3.4.5; it clears when the snapshot picks up 3.4.7.
The Leap 16.0/16.1 repos in devel:tools were already unresolvable before
this change -- they lack python313-httpx-retries and python313-uv-build
entirely, which this update does not touch.</comment>
    <requestid>1370723</requestid>
  </revision>
